# Line-ending policy — added 2026-08-03.
#
# WHY: scripts/prove-controls.sh was committed with CRLF (232 CR bytes in the blob at HEAD).
# Windows bash tolerates that; Linux bash does not, and rejects the file outright:
#   set: pipefail: invalid option name · cd: $'/work\r\r': No such file or directory
# It therefore ran green on the host and failed instantly in a Linux container. Any Linux
# execution surface — container, CI runner, WSL — hits the same wall.
#
# Executable text is pinned to LF so the committed blob is correct regardless of which
# platform writes it. Left deliberately narrow rather than `* text=auto`: a repo-wide
# normalisation would rewrite files this change has no reason to touch.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf

# Machine-generated manifests, pinned for a different reason: `swarm/agentskills_manifest`
# writes them in text mode, so regenerating on Windows rewrites every line as CRLF. A
# fifteen-line manifest change then arrives as a ~5,700-line diff, which buries the change
# and makes the `generated-agentskills` no-op gate in scripts/handoff-loop.sh unsatisfiable
# on a Windows host. Pinned by path rather than by `*.json` / `*.yaml`, keeping the narrow
# policy above: a glob here would renormalise config and fixture files this has no reason
# to touch.
agentskills.json    text eol=lf
agentskills.yaml    text eol=lf
